    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive profile, anchored by **Junior Caminero**, who commands the highest score of the day at 83.34. His matchup against Shane Baz is optimized by a massive 16% park factor boost and a dynamic platoon advantage, making him our primary engine for production. Meanwhile, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (69.12) and **Caleb Durbin** (68.33) offer exceptional upside against favorable pitching. **Caleb Durbin** specifically benefits from an elite matchup against Matt Wilkinson, whose high 8.21 xERA provides a clear path to production, while **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** capitalizes on a high-ceiling park environment that inflates his raw projection significantly. Given the premium we place on speed, **Trea Turner** (61.05) remains a mandatory start despite facing a tougher arm in Kyle Leahy, as his ability to manufacture stolen bases outweighs the moderate SP skill suppression.\n\nThe most difficult decision at the margins involved **Hector Rodriguez**, who sat just outside the starting nine with a 52.25 score. While he held a strong SP skill bonus due to his matchup against Mitch Bratt, he was ultimately relegated to the bench because his assumed #8 spot in the lineup severely throttled his potential for Runs and RBI compared to the rest of the cohort. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Kazuma Okamoto** (63.58); while his matchup metrics are strong, the 34% rain risk in his contest necessitates close monitoring as the day progresses. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** (56.07) is currently deployed as a marginal play due to an unfavorable platoon matchup against Brady Basso, though his elite xwOBA of .459 provides a high floor that keeps him active despite the efficiency dip. All rostered players, including **Dillon Dingler**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Colt Keith**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Kyle Schwarber**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Christian Yelich**, must remain monitored for lineup changes,